<title>UK: Bass Brewers CEO to join Rank - report.</title>
<headline>Bass Brewers CEO to join Rank - report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iain Napier, chief executive of Bass Plc's Bass Brewers, is set to quit to join British leisure company Rank Group Plc, the Guardian newspaper said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The report, citing company insiders, said Napier would become head of Rank's leisure division.</p>
<p>The Guardian noted that Bass faced another setback, with the expected veto by the government of its planned takeover of rival brewer Carlsberg-Tetley.</p>
<p>The report said the government was expected to rule on the takeover next week. If approved, it would make Bass Britain's biggest brewer.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
